# Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, keeps host build output from overwriting
# what the container builds. A copied-in bin/ from a Windows host is the classic cause of an image
# that runs locally and fails in CI.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/
artifacts/

**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/.turbo/

.git/
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/

**/TestResults/
**/coverage/
**/*.trx

logs/
storage/
uploads/

# Never copy secrets into an image layer. Layers are cached, distributed and trivially extractable,
# so a secret added here is a secret published even if a later layer deletes it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/secrets.json
**/*.pfx
**/*.key

docker-compose*.yml
**/Dockerfile
*.md
!README.md
